{"type":"text","timestamp":1788348328322,"sessionID":"ses_f9e260b29ffeaMqkDKkEFk3yuW","part":{"id":"prt_061ddad2a001J5iT5IgdWKRZDV","messageID":"msg_061dd85c200189NWMQCPhvt7MV","sessionID":"ses_f9e260b29ffeaMqkDKkEFk3yuW","type":"text","text":"## Static Review — MaskedScale candidate.py\n\n### Contract compliance\n\n| Check | Status | Notes |\n|-------|--------|-------|\n| Module shape | PASS | `torch`/`asc`/`asc2`/`ensure_npu_platform` at top; one public `masked_scale(x, mask, scale=1.0) -> Tensor`; three `@asc2.jit` private kernels |\n| Wrapper body | PASS | `ensure_npu_platform()` first; `x.contiguous()`/`mask.contiguous()`; `torch.empty_like(x)`; `kernel[cores](...)`; returns contiguous tensor |\n| Pinned v2 API | PASS | `asc2.global_tensor`/`copy_in`/`copy_out` with `real_shape` tails — no v1 `tensor/load/store` |\n| Kernel params | PASS | `asc.GlobalAddress` pointers; `int` sizes; `asc.ConstExpr[int]` tile; `float` scale |\n| Grid-stride loop | PASS | `asc2.range(block_idx, num_tiles, block_num, unroll_factor=2)`; tail `real_shape=[n]` |\n| Launch | PASS | `kernel[cores]` with `cores=min(72, num_tiles)`, no stream |\n| Scalars on right | PASS | `xf * mf * scale`, `mf + 256.0`, `mf < 0.0` — tile left, scalar right |\n\n### All 20 case routes\n\n| Kernel | Cases | Dispatch trigger |\n|--------|-------|-----------------|\n| `_masked_scale_float_kernel` | 3,4,8,9,12,13,18,19 | mask dtype in {f16,bf16,f32} |\n| `_masked_scale_int8_kernel` | 1,5,7,11,14,16,20 | mask dtype == int8 |\n| `_masked_scale_uint8_kernel` | 2,6,10,15,17 | mask dtype == uint8 → `mask.view(torch.int8)` + +256 fixup |\n\nAll 20 dispatch correctly. Each dtype combination JIT-specializes through one kernel source.\n\n### Critical correctness points\n\n- **int8 cast hop**: `asc2.cast(m_tile, asc.float16).to(asc.float32)` — matches verified-safe pattern; no vector op touches int8 directly\n- **uint8 +256 fixup**: applied ONLY in uint8 kernel via `asc2.where(mf < 0.0, mf + 256.0, mf)` in f32; int8 kernel has no fixup (signed, genuinely negative)\n- **Mixed-16 codegen bug (cases 3,6,16)**: only bare casts toward f32 on 16-bit tiles; no comparisons/where/arithmetic/asc2.full at f16/bf16; cast exactly once on copy_out — follows VERIFIED-SAFE rule\n- **where 256-byte rule**: TILE=2048 → 8192 bytes, 8192 % 256 == 0\n- **inf/nan (cases 12,13)**: IEEE `*` propagates; `xf * mf * scale` has same associativity as golden `x * mask * scale`; no host special-casing\n- **Zero scale (case 7)**: `finite * 0.0 = 0.0` IEEE — matches golden\n- **UB budget**: 4-5 visible f32 tiles at TILE=2048 × 1.6 × 2 unroll ≈ 105K-131K bytes, well under 253952\n\n### Design deviation (improvement, not defect)\n\nDesign specified two kernels (normal + uint8). Candidate uses three (float + int8 + uint8). This is **correct and necessary**: a single \"normal\" kernel cannot handle both int8 masks (requiring the `asc2.cast(m, f16).to(f32)` hop, since `.to(f32)` fails on int8) and float masks (where the cast hop through f16 would be lossy for bf16/f32). The three-kernel split is the correct resolution.\n\n### Anti-cheat\n\ntorch used only for: `torch.empty_like`, `.numel()`, `.contiguous()`, `.view(torch.int8)`, `.dtype` comparisons. No torch math/compute ops, no device `.to()` casts, no data_ptr caching. All numerical work inside `@asc2.jit`.\n\n### Syntax (inside @asc2.jit)\n\nNo `print`, `import`, `break`/`continue`, early `return`, exceptions, `range()`, `math.*`, `lambda`, `global`, `try/except`, nested functions. No variable scoping violations.\n\n### Gate result\n\n`python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` → **PY_COMPILE_OK**\n\nNo fixes required. Candidate is correct as-is.\n\nREVIEW_DONE","time":{"start":1788348312874,"end":1788348328319}}}
